  "runnerOnly": true,
  "reason": "Runner-only change made DURING the SC-T12 batch, after the first invocation was interrupted (the live process was started from a tool call and ended with it, after 2 model calls: call 1 answered, call 2 never returned). (1) batch.ts: the attempt AND its neuron reservation are written to the batch at dispatch, so a process that dies mid-call leaves a batch that already includes the reservation; an invocation that never recorded an end is marked interrupted; the neuron charge can be reconciled upward (never down) with a recorded reason. (2) recover.ts (new): rebuilds the answered chunks from the raw response log, accepting a response only when the SHA-256 of the exact first-attempt request matches a chunk of the frozen plan, and parses it with the Worker's own parser, so a successful chunk is never sent again. No document, label, profile, chunk plan, parser, engine, identity or comparison-rule file changed; the allowance (16 attempts, 3,000 estimated neurons) is unchanged and carries over.",
  "frozenAtCommit": "005072fb4ba270ab69c2cc31b1e04eb9c14aebdd",
